cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use REPOMIND in your research or production deployment, please cite this methodology preprint."
title: "REPOMIND: Reproducing 256K-context Repository-Scale Code Understanding on a Single AMD MI300X with FP8 KV Cache"
abstract: >-
  REPOMIND is an open-source repository-scale coding agent that operates on a single
  AMD MI300X (192 GB HBM3) at 256K context length using Qwen3-Coder-Next-FP8.
  This preprint reports 62 measured data points across 124 minutes of MI300X stress
  testing, including a per-cell AITER attention backend regression report on the
  AITER × FP8 KV cache configuration. Total session cost: $4.12 of compute on AMD
  Developer Cloud. MIT-licensed code; CC-BY-4.0 preprint.
